    "_profile_metadata": {
        "name": "Basal Ganglia Striatum - MSN Network",
        "description": "Neuron model: HODGKIN_HUXLEY (dt=0.05ms). Striatal microcircuit: 95% inhibitory MSNs (Medium Spiny Neurons), 5% FS interneurons. MSNs have hyperpolarized rest (-80mV), high spike threshold (-25mV) requiring strong cortical drive — modeled via negative OU mean current. Strong STP depression (U=0.4, tau_d=400ms) reflecting corticostriatal synaptic depression (Ding 2008). REWARD MODULATION ENABLED — critical for dopaminergic reinforcement learning in striatum. LTD-biased STDP reflecting dopamine-dependent plasticity (Shen 2008).",
        "literature": [
            "Ding et al. 2008 — Corticostriatal STP depression (U≈0.4, tau_d~400ms)",
            "Shen et al. 2008 — Dopamine-dependent bidirectional STDP in MSNs",
            "Schultz 1998 — Reward prediction error and dopamine",
            "Koos & Tepper 1999 — FS interneuron feed-forward inhibition (~5%)",
            "Wilson & Groves 1981 — MSN resting potential ~-80mV, up-state ~-50mV",
            "Izhikevich 2007 — MSN-like parameters (high rheobase, delayed firing)"
        ],
